        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 84-year-old male patient, admitted on 18/01/2013 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, physical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheezing. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated hypercapnic respiratory failure. Oxygen saturation was monitored continuously. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulized bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. He responded well to treatment with improvement of dyspnea and oxygen saturation. He is discharged in stable condition with adjusted inhaler therapy and a short course of oral steroids. Please arrange early follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Yours sincerely.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Hospital course note"
                }
              ]
